Vic,

I have SuSe Linux 7.0 and NT4.0 running on my 433a.

To install Linux I switched from Bios Settings to the VMS console.
(Bios settings / advanced settings)
After a restart (switch off & on) the Alpha starts with ">>>".
Just type "sh dev d" to get your devices listed.
To boot from your Linux-CD type "boot dka200" (dka200 is an example,
use the shown device as described above).
"help" shows all available commands (it's VMS).
"ecu" returns to Bios Settings, here it is possible to switch back the
Alpha to start with NT (again advanced settings / restart).
Define OS selection menu within Bios.

If you have problems setting up a selection menu for operating
systems, just let me know.

Before spending money you should check out if your hardware is
supported - e.g. my Matrox Millennium II does not support KDE 2.0 .
Only a few graphics adapters support NT and Linux. Even not every
Permedia2-Card does.

Regards,
Fritz


