I just finished  finally setting up rh 7.1 on my alpha 164sx. Its one thing
to have to deal with milo and setting the os boot selection -- but this
distro is just plain broken on the alpha sx 164.

First of all after making the generic.img / ramdisk images that came shipped
on the distro the alpha would load ....load ... and just as the kernel
started ... POOM reboot. I ended up wasting 3 hrs thinking it was something
I was doing wrong - I even at one point tried swappy floppy drives thinking
my floppy was nfg. Then I thought ... must be my firmware ... after dickin
around for another hr I had that updated. Nope -same problem ... okay ..
maybe it's milo --- yeah another hr milo updated and still the same problem
. Finally I figured out the default kernel wouldn't work on the alpha sx164.
Shame on you RH! I ended up using the generic.img and ramdisk.img from rh
7.0 and an ftp install.

Then after 10 hrs I got all my packages installed and ready for the moment
of truth ... Boot - POOM - kernel won't load. I had to boot back to the 2.2
kernel on the floppy and use rescue mode to rebuild the kernel. 3 more hrs
later - I had a working distro installed..... or so I thought. Then I loaded
up the installed shipped kde 2.1.2 ... POOM locked up solid after 3-4 mins
