> to have to deal with milo and setting the os boot selection -- but this
> distro is just plain broken on the alpha sx 164.

Release notes for that distro mention that detail that booting it
from milo is "not supported".  The problem is this line in a kernel
configuration:

  CONFIG_ALPHA_LEGACY_START_ADDRESS

It has to be set if you are booting from milo but not set for
some high-end machines (or they will not boot).  Officially Red Hat
bothers only with SRM console.  You can make it work with ARC and
milo but as far as Red Hat is concerned you are mostly on your own.

> I'm posting this for 2 reasons:

> 1] I hope to save others a lot of time and grief and maybe some of thier
> sanity.

This may be a good reason if somebody, like you, would bother to check
and read these things in archives.  Installation problems, and ways to
work around them, were discussed multiple times on this list, with
details.  It is nice that you managed to get things up on your own but
you could save a lot of time and effort by doing a bit of a reserch
first.

BTW - RH 7.1 with current updates is quite a bit different system then
the original 7.1 distro in various aspects.  Yes, you still need an
updated custom kernel if you are booting from milo.

  --mj


