Paul you identified the problem as 'libcurses.so'...

>> [XXXXX distribfold]$ ./foldit
>> 4320:./foldtrajlite: : Fatal Error: cannot map libcurses.so
>> [XXXXX distribfold]$
>> 
>> curses is installed on this box, anything I can do to force this
>> binary to run under linux???

The binary doesn't have it and you cannot dynamically link a Tru64
binary
to the RedHat 'libcurses' that you have and libcurses is NOT in
the 'Tru64-compat' rpm. (do 'rpm -qil Tru64-compat' to see what is in
there)
You have two choices persuade them to link 'libcurses' into the binary,
or build a local libcurses from the RedHat sources and link as a
dynamically
linked shared library in COFF format ('ld' on the alpha can do this)
the RedHat libcurses is an ELF shared object. A "normal" user program
should not care where the kernel symbols are,
Netscape and Acrobat use the compatibility library to write in X
windows,
do 'man ncurses' to see what curses is all about,
Stephen Lewis

