> 433a? Should I buy this from Compaq?

You don't need anything to buy from Compaq. 
If you want to run linux you have to take care of your graphics adapter. If 
you got a powerstorm adapter you won't get a driver for xfree for it, then 
you have to use Tru64 to get the card running. In my oppinion Tru64 is 
anyway the unix to choose for alpha workstations. You ca buy a "enthausiast 
version" for 99$ from Compaq. If you got a Matrox Millenium for example you 
have to possible ways to install linux.
Under SRM (you have a >>> prompt) you can use aboot. But if you are trying 
to install WinNT you are probaly under AlphaBios. From there you can use 
milo. Be aware that you /boot  partition is FAT16. The best would be if you 
get a distribution and read the install instructions.

> What about NT 4.0? I tried to re-install NT 4.0 from the CD but it doesn't
> seem to recognize the processor and provides a list of processors, which
> does not include the Alpha 21164 processor. Any clues?
You should be able to install WinNT 4.0, but you will probably get more 
applications for  Linux or Tru64 or VMS.

